Sign-in now has a working **Forgot password?** path, and I drove it end to end in a browser.

### What changed

- [client.ts](apps/web/src/lib/cloud/client.ts#L243-L256) — new `cloudAuth.forgotPassword(email)`. It is deliberately unauthenticated (no bearer token, no session) and goes through the existing sidecar egress route like every other cloud call, so a filtered network still gets the proxy diagnosis rather than a vague failure. A non-2xx becomes a `CloudError`, so a `rate_limited` answer is shown instead of a fake success.
- [AccountPage.tsx](apps/web/src/features/account/AccountPage.tsx) — the sign-in card gains a small “Forgot password?” link under the password field. It switches to a reset view with only an email field, “Email me a reset link”, and “Back to sign in”; a successful request replaces the form with a neutral confirmation (“If an account exists for *address*, a reset link is on its way”, 30-minute validity, spam hint) — worded so the screen can’t be used to probe which addresses have accounts. Failures use the same honest sentence as sign-in, including the Worker’s “Too many reset requests”. Register mode and the existing toggles are untouched.

### Verification (not just a green build)

- `npx tsc --noEmit` in `apps/web` → **exit 0**; the full web suite → **39 files, 352 tests passed** (new file [cloudForgotPassword.test.ts](apps/web/test/cloudForgotPassword.test.ts) asserts the exact egress path/method, that **no** `Authorization` header is sent, and that 429 and transport failures surface as errors).
- `eslint` on both changed source files → **exit 0**.
- Browser run against the real stack (local sidecar + Vite): `/account` rendered “Welcome back”; clicking **Forgot password?** produced the email-only reset view; submitting `no-reset-probe-20261024@resend.dev` produced the neutral confirmation, and the network log shows `POST /api/v1/cloud/egress → 200` — i.e. the request really reached the production Worker. The address has no account, so intentionally **no email was sent and no new `reset.requested` row appeared** in production audit (last row is still the `mail_sent` from the earlier delivery test). Register mode and “Back to sign in” were re-checked afterwards.
- The dev API (8787) and Vite (5173) processes I started for that run were stopped; both ports are free. No accounts or other production rows were created.

Nothing is deployed from this change — it’s the desktop/web client, so it ships with the next app build rather than a Worker deploy.

If you want the reset path to feel finished, the remaining rough edge is telling a throttled user when they can retry.
