The adaptive intelligence system is implemented, wired into the real connect path, and measured — with the one criterion that could not be settled on this machine reported as such rather than claimed.

**What now exists (working tree, not deployed):**

- **Policy core** — [packages/shared/src/adaptive/](packages/shared/src/adaptive/): decayed evidence, contextual-bandit ranking with a UCB-style exploration bonus capped by policy, failure classifier, signed-manifest verification, research-candidate registry. Pure, dependency-free, no network call anywhere (so no external AI API is ever needed).
- **Engine service** — [adaptiveEngine.ts](apps/api/src/services/adaptiveEngine.ts): the approved-strategy list comes from `findEngineBinary` plus the tunnel's own `engineSupports`/`engineSupportsConfig` predicates, so the engine can only reorder cores that are installed and compatible — never add a node, hostname or credential. Learn/decide/status/reset, plus signed policy install with revocation and rollback. Trust anchor is real Ed25519 ([adaptiveManifestTrust.ts](apps/api/src/services/adaptiveManifestTrust.ts)).
- **Real connect path** — [autoConnect.ts](apps/api/src/services/autoConnect.ts): `quickConnectCore` dials the order the engine returns, records outcomes only from the tunnel's verification (an exit IP actually read through it), and now tries one more approved core before abandoning a node.
- **API + UI** — [routes/adaptive.ts](apps/api/src/routes/adaptive.ts) (`status`, `plan` dry-run with per-position explanations, `reset`, `policy`, `policy/rollback`) and [AdaptiveRecoveryCard.tsx](apps/web/src/features/vpn/AdaptiveRecoveryCard.tsx) in the VPN shell: learned strategies with honest sample counts, why-each-core-is-unusable reasons, both switches, and one-click **clear local learning data**.

**Two real defects the new tests caught and I fixed:** `plan()` compared engine ids against strategy ids, so a fresh install would have been reordered alphabetically instead of left alone; and a failed learned core abandoned the node instead of trying the next approved one.

**Verification actually run:** 57 shared adaptive tests, 24 engine/manifest tests (real signatures, tampering, expiry, revocation, rollback), 5 integration tests through `quickConnectCore` (the dialled core really changes; a started core with no verified traffic is a failure), 33 pre-existing connect-path/route tests, clean typechecks in api/web/shared, and a live corpus — a real local Xray REALITY server probed by the machine's real xray/sing-box cores through the app's own probe path: 24 real attempts, 12 comparable episodes, baseline and adaptive both 100% first-attempt success at p50 933 ms / p95 1045 ms.

**What I did not verify, per the report:** criterion 12 (adaptive *outperforming* baseline) is **NOT TESTED** — every corpus available here is a parity corpus, because this machine's public node list carried no traffic in 24/24 attempts and a fabricated failing core would not be a real measurement. DNS classification is covered; leak/kill-switch routing suites were not re-run; CPU/heap profiling is not done; the UI card is typechecked but not visually exercised. Full detail, including the metric I had to fix because it flattered the wrong party, is in [ADAPTIVE_EVIDENCE_2026-10-26.md](reports/adaptive/ADAPTIVE_EVIDENCE_2026-10-26.md) with raw corpus in [REPLAY_LIVE_REALITY.json](reports/adaptive/REPLAY_LIVE_REALITY.json); the journal and [task ledger](tmp/NETPULSE_TASK_LEDGER.md) now carry the open items. Nothing was deployed, and exploration stays off by default.
