Now the record file must be fresh per run: Driver::start deletes any existing file, and sets the env var. Drop removes it on success (like the driver log), keeps it on failure and prints the path? On panic, print the rows in the failure message... Hmm, the failure messages should include the record contents for diagnosis. Add a method `record_summary()` returning the parsed rows pretty-printed, used in panic messages.

