The adaptive-agent work is finished and verified. Here is what actually changed and what it does.

## What the agent now reports while it works

Every quick-connect run gets its own activity topic (`quick-connect:<runId>`) and the tunnel service publishes real milestones into it as they happen: `preparing`, `handoff`, `memory-check`, `adaptive-plan`, `adaptive-choice`, `discovery-start`, `candidate-probe`, `attempt-start`, `core-start`, `core-ready` / `core-failed`, `dns-policy-active`, `relay-check`, `dns-response`, `verification-failed`, `route-active`, `complete`. These are emitted from the code that actually performs the step — [proxyTunnel.ts](apps/api/src/services/proxyTunnel.ts) and [autoConnect.ts](apps/api/src/services/autoConnect.ts) — not synthesized on a timer, and the panel reads them over the existing ticket-gated WebSocket.

## The visual part you asked for

A new animated six-hop path renders above the log: **Request → Policy → Core → DNS → TLS trace → Egress**. The hop the agent is on pulses with a travelling dot on the rail; completed hops turn solid green; a failed core or verification turns red. When the agent is at the DNS hop, that chip gets its own pinging resolver dot and reads “Core configured with DoH policy; response not yet observed”, then “Hostname resolved inside the tunneled request”.

The important accuracy rule baked in: an armed DNS policy is **not** a resolution. Only `dns-response` — a hostname resolved inside a real tunneled HTTPS request — turns the DNS hop green, and the footnote still says the resolver itself was not independently identified. A second attempt resets the attempt-scoped hops, so an old failure never lingers on screen while a retry is in flight. All motion is gated behind `motion-safe:` with `motion-reduce:animate-none`, and the hop states are exposed as `data-state` for assistive tech and tests.

Files: [AgentPathTrace.tsx](apps/web/src/features/vpn/AgentPathTrace.tsx) (visual), [agentPath.ts](apps/web/src/features/vpn/agentPath.ts) (pure derivation), [QuickConnectActivity.tsx](apps/web/src/features/vpn/QuickConnectActivity.tsx) (now hosts the path plus the event log and telemetry), rendered from [ProxyTunnelCard.tsx](apps/web/src/features/vpn/ProxyTunnelCard.tsx).

## Verified

- `apps/web/test/agentPath.test.ts` — 7/7: pending run stays pending, DNS policy never completes the DNS hop, tunneled response completes DNS + trace, exit address only after `route-active`, failure resets on retry.
- `apps/web/test/agentPathRender.test.tsx` — 3/3: rendered `data-state` separates armed policy from observed resolution, no resolver is named, reduced-motion classes present.
- `apps/api/test/adaptiveConnect.test.ts` — 7/7 (includes the “a started core is not a working tunnel” case).
